      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1979, Lemont earned a place on the National Register of Historic Places, honoring its rural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lemontvillage.org/historic-lemont",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Bellefonte Central Railroad once powered Lemont's boom, and today the town offers historic railroad speeder rides.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Granary, Pennsylvania's last remaining granary, now hosts art shows and community events in Lemont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Lemont Village Association, founded in 1979, fights to preserve historic buildings and keep the post office in town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lemontvillage.org/historic-lemont",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
